That's true (as `module.exports`) of the outermost context in intro.js (which calls the IIFE), but _not_ true of the IIFE context (which defines `module.exports`) or the `factory` context (which defines and returns `jQuery`). So we could either add `setTimeout` etc. parameters to `factory`, or define `setTimeout = window.setTimeout || this.setTimeout` etc. _in_ `factory`. I'm inclined towards the former, which won't even break in strict mode. And which is practically indistinguishable from your proposal anyway.
